    74	  inform investigation and select among registered branches, as A9.2 permits.
    75	- **V1's accepted limit:** when both authority channels are captured, receipts under the captor's own keys pass.
    76	- H2 is not adjudicated.
    77	
    78	## Still to do (owner, unless marked)
    79	
    80	- **By 13 Nov:** E10 extraction.
    81	- **By 20 Nov:** the V1 issuer on AWS behind an API; the service verifier; P3's assumption half; E10 vectors run
    82	  against AWS; the P9 code inspection and its outstanding execution evidence, including the two-machine vector;
    83	  bounded local refusal; A9.4's missing-capture negative control; H3 measured.
    84	- **Before the first public verifier release** (A10.4.2):
    85	  - the custody procedure and its rehearsal;
    86	  - the production release key;
    87	  - the fingerprint channels, named by the author, independent of the operational environment by role and
    88	    credential (row 6);
    89	  - the release-format test vectors;
    90	  - the GCP VPC Service Controls perimeter;
    91	  - a policy for responses the signer was not asked for (E-06).
    92	- **4 Dec:** the relying-party test and the dead-service test. Ship or stop is the author's decision.
