    10	**Why these cases are not in `formal/p8/vectors`.** The P8 codecs A (`gen.py`) and B (`check.py`) are
    11	**candidate-codec and cryptographic-profile evidence** only:
    12	- both hard-code the classical id and the pair id in one codec registry;
    13	- both treat registry membership as the condition for verifying signatures;
    14	- neither has an input for the selected catalog id or for the registration state.
    15	
    16	So they cannot test the routing below. These cases need the profile verifier: its catalog, its registration state
    17	and its row-ordered verdict.
    18	
    19	The pair id throughout is `KMS-MLDSA65-PURE-GPG-OPENPGP4-ECDSA-P256-SHA256`, and the classical id is
    20	`OPENPGP4-ECDSA-P256-SHA256`. Neither the pair id nor the r2-F01 routing rule is altered by these cases.
    21	
    22	## Cases
    23	
    24	**(a) Before registration: the hybrid id is absent.**
    25	- Installation: the hybrid supplement is not registered. The catalog id is the classical one.
    26	- Input: a receipt and manifest whose frames carry the pair id consistently, with nonempty signatures in both
    27	  slots.
    28	  - Variant a1: a 3309-byte kms signature.
